| Milestone | Exit evidence |
|---|---|
| Documentation foundation | Schema, navigation, links, search, and static build pass |
| Broker prototype | Informal request reaches a simulated impact result |
| Agent contract foundation | Exactly eight role contracts and source hashes validate in CI |
| Telemetry recording foundation | Provider usage normalization, redaction, strict schemas, local/CI sinks, and malformed/failure tests pass |
| Context preflight/compiler | Determinism, reference-first retrieval, deduplication, exact-data preservation, budgets, and stable-prefix tests pass |
| Agent eval foundation | Sixteen required families and result schema validate; deterministic and live lanes remain separate |
| Tool policy gateway | Role-aware allow/ask/deny decisions and bypass tests pass independently of prompt compliance |
| Provider adapter contracts | Claude, OpenAI, and Codex CLI responses/errors normalize into the same domain records |
| Council/risk engine | Risk 0–3 lane counts, reviewer independence, cross-provider review, and blocker semantics pass |
| Evidence-gated tuning | Unevaluated role configuration remains frozen and candidate guardrail tests pass |
| Agent publication CI | Diff-bound author/QA/review evidence and uniquely named required checks validate |
| Release/provenance definitions | Build attestation, same-artifact promotion, post-deploy evidence, and rollback workflows validate locally |
| Automatic run evidence | Representative live Claude/Codex records populate the telemetry foundation without manual copying |
| One-agent execution | One live provider runs one bounded low-risk unit with full audit |
| Second voice | Other provider reviews without sharing the author session |
| Deterministic gates | Real repository commands block completion on failure |
| Worktree isolation | Changes occur only in a verified isolated worktree |
| Human approval service | High-impact state cannot advance without recorded authority |
| Operations loop | Health, failure, cost, latency, and outcomes are measured |

The milestones above distinguish implementation from evidence. The local platform definitions through release/rollback exist; automatic run evidence, live baselines, external production approval, real promotion verification, and rollback-drill evidence remain open.
